    "['eth-trunk [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ae1 unit 0 family inet address 10.40.1.2/24\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, link aggregation is configured using `ae` (aggregated Ethernet) interfaces instead of `Eth-Trunk`.\\n2. Each physical interface is assigned to the AE group using `ether-options 802.3ad` (Juniper's equivalent to LACP).\\n3. The IP address that was on Eth-Trunk1 in Huawei is moved to the `ae1` interface in Juniper.\\n4. Note that the static routes referencing Eth-Trunk1 would need to be updated to reference ae1 in a complete Juniper translation.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ae1 unit 0 family inet address 10.40.1.2/24\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, link aggregation is configured using `ae` (aggregated Ethernet) interfaces instead of `Eth-Trunk`.\\n2. Each physical interface is assigned to the AE group using `ether-options 802.3ad` (Juniper's equivalent to LACP).\\n3. The IP address that was on Eth-Trunk1 in Huawei is moved to the `ae1` interface in Juniper.\\n4. Note that the static routes referencing Eth-Trunk1 would need to be updated to reference ae1 in a complete Juniper translation.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ae1 unit 0 family inet address 10.40.1.2/24', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ae1 unit 0 family inet address 10.40.1.2/24\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, link aggregation is configured using `ae` (aggregated Ethernet) interfaces instead of `Eth-Trunk`.\\n2. Each physical interface is assigned to the AE group using `ether-options 802.3ad` (Juniper's equivalent to LACP).\\n3. The IP address that was on Eth-Trunk1 in Huawei is moved to the `ae1` interface in Juniper.\\n4. Note that the static routes referencing Eth-Trunk1 would need to be updated to reference ae1 in a complete Juniper translation.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ae1 unit 0 family inet address 10.40.1.2/24'}]]": 1,
    "['eth-trunk [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ae1 aggregated-ether-options lacp active\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, `eth-trunk 1` translates to adding interfaces to an Aggregated Ethernet (AE) bundle, which is Juniper's equivalent of an Eth-Trunk.\\n2. The commands:\\n   - Assign physical interfaces (ge-3/0/0 and ge-4/0/0) to AE bundle 1\\n   - Configure LACP in active mode (similar to Huawei's default Eth-Trunk behavior)\\n3. Note: The IP address configuration for the AE interface would be separate, similar to how it's configured on the Eth-Trunk in Huawei.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-3/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1\\nset interfaces ae1 aggregated-ether-options lacp active\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, `eth-trunk 1` translates to adding interfaces to an Aggregated Ethernet (AE) bundle, which is Juniper's equivalent of an Eth-Trunk.\\n2. The commands:\\n   - Assign physical interfaces (ge-3/0/0 and ge-4/0/0) to AE bundle 1\\n   - Configure LACP in active mode (similar to Huawei's default Eth-Trunk behavior)\\n3. Note: The IP address configuration for the AE interface would be separate, similar to how it's configured on the Eth-Trunk in Huawei.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-4/0/0 ether-options 802.3ad ae1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ae1 aggregated-ether-options la